[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ARCH-CP-SCOPE
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Server-bound clientId + mandatory client_id / RLS
STATEMENT: >>>
Active clientId lives on the server session (not only in browser local storage). Business services and the data layer enforce client scope: every query carries a mandatory client_id predicate (repository filter and/or Postgres RLS). Search, audit, catalogs, grants, and imprint reads never cross clients. Least privilege cannot be bypassed by crafting URLs. Cross-client denial beds: FIX-DENY-CROSS-CLIENT / FIX-DENY-AUDIT-CROSS-CLIENT.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
KIND: requirement
BASE_UID: ARCH-CP-SCOPE
VERSION_N: 0
rbac_op: client:scope:select
priority: 5
iteration: iter-r0
security.catalog_ref: REQAML-SEC-SCOPE
security.verification_note: Maps to ReqAML project catalog SCOPE item.
edge: ← refines from A03
in_scope_of_contract: Design-2026-10
in_scope_of_contract: Security package
delivered_by_release: R1-core-ALM
edge: → uses to CAP-SCOPED-VIEW (RELATIONS TYPE: Child; Parent would cycle)
edge: → conforms_to to AC-3 (pin imprint=nist-800-53@rev5-dogfood-20261006)
<<<
