[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ARCH-CAT-MIGRATE
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Migrate pins: preview, .N for locked, in-place drafts
STATEMENT: >>>
Migrate-to-imprint apply rules (locked decision): (1) Preview is mandatory — classify each affected pin's item change as editorial | normative | withdrawn | renumbered; the operator must accept before apply (dry-run; no silent apply). (2) Locked requirement versions — DERIVED (no first-class flag): a version is locked when status≠draft AND (referenced by any contract.in_scope_of OR any release.delivers). Locked pins migrate only by minting successor .N versions that ConformsTo the new (imprint_id, item_uid); never rewrite the frozen version in place. (3) Draft / unlocked versions may retarget the pin in place after preview accept (still no auto without accept). (4) Steward/Security gates apply; AO may approve-only on locked migrate (permission-tree); migration is audited. Aligns with catalog_imprints, conforms_to.catalog_imprint_id, catalog_drift, and ARCH-LOCKED Locked migrate uses mint_kind=pin successor (ARCH-MINT-KIND); clears approval; requires gate_signoff then re-approve (ARCH-GATE-SIGNOFF).
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
KIND: requirement
BASE_UID: ARCH-CAT-MIGRATE
VERSION_N: 0
rbac_op: catalog:imprint:migrate:apply
priority: 55
iteration: iter-r2
security.catalog_ref: REQAML-SEC-CATALOG
security.verification_note: Catalog steward gates; standard catalogs imprint-published read-only. AC-3/CM-5 aligned. Pins are (imprint_id, item_uid). Migrate requires preview accept + Steward/Security gate; audited.
edge: → conforms_to to AC-3 (pin imprint=nist-800-53@rev5-dogfood-20261006)
edge: → conforms_to to CM-5 (pin imprint=nist-800-53@rev5-dogfood-20261006)
edge: → conforms_to to AU-2 (pin imprint=nist-800-53@rev5-dogfood-20261006)
edge: → conforms_to to AU-12 (pin imprint=nist-800-53@rev5-dogfood-20261006)
<<<
